IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ita-types`

-- Income Tax Act 2007 (UK) — THE THREE GOALS.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2007-3.txt.

§ `Rules`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`at least nil` a MEANS IF a GREATER THAN 0 THEN a ELSE 0

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded up to a whole pound` x MEANS 0 MINUS FLOOR (0 MINUS x)

-- The part of the slice of income from `lo` to `hi` that falls between `a`
-- and `b`.
GIVEN lo IS A NUMBER, hi IS A NUMBER, a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part from` lo `to` hi `between` a `and` b MEANS
    `at least nil` (`the smaller of` hi `and` b MINUS (IF lo GREATER THAN a THEN lo ELSE a))

§§ `Goal 1 — personal allowance (ss 35, 58)`

-- s 415, 58(2): "grossed up by reference to the basic rate".
@ref ss 58(2), 415
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the grossed up Gift Aid of` t MEANS
    t's `Gift Aid paid` TIMES 100 DIVIDED BY (100 MINUS t's `rates`'s `basic rate`)

-- s 58(1): net income, less the grossed-up Gift Aid (Step 2) and the gross
-- relief-at-source pension contributions (Step 3).
@ref s 58(1)
@export My adjusted net income under s 58 of the Income Tax Act 2007 (UK): my net income less the grossed-up amount of my Gift Aid donations and the gross amount of my relief-at-source pension contributions. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`  @desc My income, Gift Aid and pension contributions, and the basic rate
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my adjusted net income` t MEANS
        t's `non-savings income` PLUS t's `savings income` PLUS t's `dividend income`
    MINUS `the grossed up Gift Aid of` t
    MINUS t's `gross pension contributions`

-- s 55B(4)-(5): 10% of the s 35(1) allowance, rounded up to a multiple of
-- £10.
@ref s 55B(4)-(5)
`the transferable amount` MEANS 10 TIMES (`rounded up to a whole pound` (12570 DIVIDED BY 10 DIVIDED BY 10))

-- s 35(1)-(3): £12,570, reduced by one-half of the excess of adjusted net
-- income over £100,000, rounded up to a multiple of £1. s 55B(6): reduced by
-- the transferable amount where I elected to transfer it.
@ref ss 35, 55B(6)
@export My personal allowance under s 35 of the Income Tax Act 2007 (UK): £12,570, less half the amount by which my adjusted net income exceeds £100,000 (rounded up to a whole pound, not below nil), and less the transferable amount if I have elected to transfer it to my spouse or civil partner (s 55B(6)). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`  @desc My income, Gift Aid, pension contributions and any marriage allowance election
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my personal allowance` t MEANS
    IF t's `marriage allowance` EQUALS `I elected to transfer my allowance`
    THEN `at least nil` (tapered MINUS `the transferable amount`)
    ELSE tapered
    WHERE
        excess MEANS `at least nil` (`my adjusted net income` t MINUS 100000)
        tapered MEANS `at least nil` (`rounded up to a whole pound` (12570 MINUS excess DIVIDED BY 2))

§§ `Goal 2 — income tax liability (ss 10-16, 23)`

-- s 10(5), (5A), (6), 414(2)(b): the basic rate limit £37,700 and the higher
-- rate limit (2 × £12,570 + £100,000), each increased by the grossed-up Gift
-- Aid and the gross pension contributions.
@ref ss 10(5)-(6), 414(2)
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my basic rate limit` t MEANS 37700 PLUS `the grossed up Gift Aid of` t PLUS t's `gross pension contributions`

@ref ss 10(5A)-(6), 414(2)
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my higher rate limit` t MEANS (2 TIMES 12570) PLUS 100000 PLUS `the grossed up Gift Aid of` t PLUS t's `gross pension contributions`

-- s 23 Step 3, s 25(3A): the allowance comes off non-savings income first.
-- Between savings and dividends, s 25(2): "in the way which will result in
-- the greatest reduction in the taxpayer's liability" — both orders are
-- worked out and the one giving less tax is taken (F1, changed after the
-- independent pass). `df` is TRUE where the rest of the allowance goes
-- against dividends before savings.
@ref ss 23, 25(2), (3A)
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my taxable non-savings income` t MEANS `at least nil` (t's `non-savings income` MINUS `my personal allowance` t)

GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the allowance left after non-savings income for` t MEANS `at least nil` (`my personal allowance` t MINUS t's `non-savings income`)

GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`, df IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my taxable savings income` t `ordered` df MEANS
    IF df
    THEN `at least nil` (t's `savings income` MINUS `at least nil` (left MINUS t's `dividend income`))
    ELSE `at least nil` (t's `savings income` MINUS left)
    WHERE
        left MEANS `the allowance left after non-savings income for` t

GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`, df IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my taxable dividend income` t `ordered` df MEANS
    IF df
    THEN `at least nil` (t's `dividend income` MINUS left)
    ELSE `at least nil` (t's `dividend income` MINUS `at least nil` (left MINUS t's `savings income`))
    WHERE
        left MEANS `the allowance left after non-savings income for` t

-- The total taxable income is the same in either order.
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my taxable income` t MEANS `my taxable non-savings income` t PLUS `my taxable savings income` t `ordered` FALSE PLUS `my taxable dividend income` t `ordered` FALSE

-- Tax on the slice of income from `lo` to `hi` at three rates by band.
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`, lo IS A NUMBER, hi IS A NUMBER, r1 IS A NUMBER, r2 IS A NUMBER, r3 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`tax for` t `on the slice from` lo `to` hi `at` r1 `,` r2 `,` r3 MEANS
    (     `the part from` lo `to` hi `between` 0 `and` brl TIMES r1
     PLUS `the part from` lo `to` hi `between` brl `and` hrl TIMES r2
     PLUS (IF hi GREATER THAN hrl THEN (hi MINUS (IF lo GREATER THAN hrl THEN lo ELSE hrl)) ELSE 0) TIMES r3)
    DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        brl MEANS `my basic rate limit` t
        hrl MEANS `my higher rate limit` t

-- s 12: the starting rate for savings (0%) on income up to £5,000 so far as
-- it is savings income, savings being above non-savings income (s 16).
@ref ss 12, 16
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`, df IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my savings at the starting rate` t `ordered` df MEANS
    `at least nil` (`the smaller of` (`my taxable savings income` t `ordered` df) `and` (5000 MINUS `my taxable non-savings income` t))

-- s 12B: £1,000 with no higher-rate income, £500 with higher-rate but no
-- additional-rate income, nil with additional-rate income (income that would
-- be so charged but for the nil rates counts; savings in the savings higher
-- and additional bands count as higher-rate and additional-rate income, F5).
@ref s 12B
@export My savings allowance under s 12B of the Income Tax Act 2007 (UK): £1,000 if none of my income is higher-rate income, £500 if some is but none is additional-rate income, and nil if some is additional-rate income. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`  @desc My income and the limits
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my savings allowance` t MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `my taxable income` t GREATER THAN `my higher rate limit` t THEN 0
        IF `my taxable income` t GREATER THAN `my basic rate limit` t  THEN 500
        OTHERWISE                                                         1000

-- s 12A: the savings nil rate on so much of the savings above the starting
-- rate limit as does not exceed the savings allowance.
@ref s 12A
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`, df IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my savings at the savings nil rate` t `ordered` df MEANS
    `the smaller of` (`my taxable savings income` t `ordered` df MINUS `my savings at the starting rate` t `ordered` df) `and` (`my savings allowance` t)

@ref ss 10, 11D, 12, 12A, 13, 13A, 16, 23 Steps 4-5
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`, df IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my tax before reductions` t `ordered` df MEANS
        `tax for` t `on the slice from` 0 `to` n `at` (r's `basic rate`) `,` (r's `higher rate`) `,` (r's `additional rate`)
    PLUS `tax for` t `on the slice from` (n PLUS `my savings at the starting rate` t `ordered` df PLUS `my savings at the savings nil rate` t `ordered` df) `to` (n PLUS s) `at` (r's `savings basic rate`) `,` (r's `savings higher rate`) `,` (r's `savings additional rate`)
    PLUS `tax for` t `on the slice from` (n PLUS s PLUS `the smaller of` d `and` 500) `to` (n PLUS s PLUS d) `at` 10.75 `,` 35.75 `,` 39.35
    WHERE
        r MEANS t's `rates`
        n MEANS `my taxable non-savings income` t
        s MEANS `my taxable savings income` t `ordered` df
        d MEANS `my taxable dividend income` t `ordered` df

-- s 25(2): the order giving the greatest reduction.
@ref s 25(2)
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dividends first is better for` t IF
    `my tax before reductions` t `ordered` TRUE LESS THAN `my tax before reductions` t `ordered` FALSE

GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my taxable savings income` t MEANS `my taxable savings income` t `ordered` (`dividends first is better for` t)

GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my taxable dividend income` t MEANS `my taxable dividend income` t `ordered` (`dividends first is better for` t)

GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my savings at the starting rate` t MEANS `my savings at the starting rate` t `ordered` (`dividends first is better for` t)

GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my savings at the savings nil rate` t MEANS `my savings at the savings nil rate` t `ordered` (`dividends first is better for` t)

@ref ss 10, 11D, 12, 12A, 13, 13A, 16, 23 Steps 4-5, 25(2)
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my tax before reductions` t MEANS `my tax before reductions` t `ordered` (`dividends first is better for` t)

@ref ss 10, 11D, 12, 12A, 13, 13A, 16, 23 Steps 4-6
@export My income tax liability for the year under the Income Tax Act 2007 (UK): the allowance set against non-savings income first and then against savings or dividends in whichever order gives less tax; non-savings income, then savings, then dividends, taxed through the bands (the basic rate limit £37,700 and higher rate limit £125,140, each extended by grossed-up Gift Aid and gross pension contributions), with the starting rate for savings on up to £5,000, the savings allowance and the first £500 of dividends at nil rates (still using up the bands), dividends at 10.75%, 35.75% and 39.35%, less any marriage allowance tax reduction. The basic, higher and additional rates (and the savings rates) are those set by Parliament for the year. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`  @desc The rates, my income, Gift Aid, pension contributions and any marriage allowance election
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my income tax liability` t MEANS
    `at least nil` (`my tax before reductions` t MINUS `my marriage allowance reduction` t)

§§ `Goal 3 — marriage allowance (ss 55B-55C)`

-- The same taxpayer with a different marriage allowance position.
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`, m IS A `Marriage allowance role`
GIVETH A `Taxpayer`
`the taxpayer` t `with the role` m MEANS
    `Taxpayer` OF t's `rates`, t's `non-savings income`, t's `savings income`, t's `dividend income`, t's `Gift Aid paid`, t's `gross pension contributions`, m

-- ss 55B(2)(b)-(ba), 55C(1)(c)-(ca): not liable at any rate other than the
-- basic rate and the rates listed, which include the savings nil rate and
-- the dividend nil rate; but dividends that would be at the upper or
-- additional rate but for the dividend nil rate count against it. So:
-- non-savings income within the basic rate limit; no savings charged above it
-- except at the starting or savings nil rate; and no dividends above it (F6,
-- changed after the independent pass).
@ref ss 55B(2)(b)-(ba), 55C(1)(c)-(ca)
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I pay no more than the basic rate` t IF
        n AT MOST brl
    AND (n PLUS s) AT MOST (IF brl GREATER THAN chargedFrom THEN brl ELSE chargedFrom)
    AND (d EQUALS 0 OR n PLUS s PLUS d AT MOST brl)
    WHERE
        brl MEANS `my basic rate limit` t
        n MEANS `my taxable non-savings income` t
        s MEANS `my taxable savings income` t
        d MEANS `my taxable dividend income` t
        chargedFrom MEANS n PLUS `my savings at the starting rate` t PLUS `my savings at the savings nil rate` t

-- s 55C(1)(b)-(c): entitled to a personal allowance and, with it reduced by
-- the transferable amount, liable at no rate above the basic rate. (The
-- net-income condition in s 55C(2) applies only to those resident under
-- s 56(3), outside this encoding's seat.)
@ref s 55C(1)
@export May I elect to transfer part of my personal allowance to my spouse or civil partner, under s 55C of the Income Tax Act 2007 (UK)? Yes if I am entitled to a personal allowance and, with it reduced by the transferable amount, I would pay tax at no rate above the basic rate. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`  @desc My income, assumed with the election in force
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I may elect to transfer my allowance` t IF
        `my personal allowance` (`the taxpayer` t `with the role` `no election`) GREATER THAN 0
    AND `I pay no more than the basic rate` (`the taxpayer` t `with the role` `I elected to transfer my allowance`)

-- s 55B(1)-(4): the gaining party's tax reduction is the basic rate of the
-- transferable amount, if it pays no more than the basic rate; given at
-- Step 6, so not more than the tax before it.
@ref s 55B(1)-(4)
@export My marriage allowance tax reduction as the gaining party under s 55B of the Income Tax Act 2007 (UK): the basic rate of the transferable amount (£1,260), if my spouse or civil partner has elected and I pay no more than the basic rate; not more than my tax before it. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`  @desc My income, the basic rate and whether my spouse or civil partner elected
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my marriage allowance reduction` t MEANS
    IF t's `marriage allowance` EQUALS `my spouse or civil partner elected to transfer to me` AND `I pay no more than the basic rate` t
    THEN `the smaller of` (`the transferable amount` TIMES t's `rates`'s `basic rate` DIVIDED BY 100) `and` (`my tax before reductions` t)
    ELSE 0
